Can't use matrix calculations in our indicator tool

Our indicator tool uses `oakscriptjs` for PineScript-compatible technical analysis. I want to keep groups of indicator values in matrices so I can rearrange the data and combine calculations through the same package. The `matrix` namespace in `src/matrix/index.ts` looks like the right fit. Here's a small example of how we'd use it:

```typescript
import { matrix } from 'oakscriptjs';
const samples = matrix.new_matrix(2, 3, 0);
matrix.set(samples, 0, 1, 7);
matrix.set(samples, 1, 2, 11);
const byColumn = matrix.transpose(samples);
const secondColumn = matrix.row(byColumn, 1);
```

The documented behavior would let this code create and populate a matrix, transpose it, and read the resulting row. Instead, it stops at matrix creation with `"not implemented"`.

Could you implement the remaining matrix stubs in `src/matrix/index.ts`, including the documented manipulation, arithmetic, statistics, matrix checks and linear algebra operations? Their signatures and doc comments describe the public API; algorithm descriptions are guidance. Follow the observable behavior, including the `CHANGELOG.md` rules for `matrix.get`/`matrix.set` with na indices and for `matrix.rank`. The numerical rank convention takes precedence over the older row-reduction description. `docs/inventory.md` also lists the API under “matrix (Matrix Operations)”. Keep the existing public API names because the package's tests import them, and keep the package's own
